            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "There is no legal definition. It usually means the protein comes from a food that has only been dried, pressed or milled, such as hemp seed, pumpkin seed or egg white, or a blend of recognizable foods. Some brands use it for isolates with added vegetable powders, so read the ingredient list."
