          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is protein powder ultra-processed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Under the NOVA system used in much ultra-processed food research, protein isolates mark a food as ultra-processed, so most commercial powders count. That describes processing, not nutritional value. Single-ingredient powders such as milled hemp seed or dried egg white are much closer to minimally processed foods."
