          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whole food protein powder is a marketing phrase, not a standard, so judge every tub by its ingredient list. Just Ingredients is the best whole-food-style blend for taste, and Sprout Living pumpkin seed, Nutiva hemp, Naked Egg, Simply Tera's plain whey and PB2 Performance are single foods with very little done to them.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Expect less protein per scoop the closer a powder stays to its source, and compare on cost per 25 g of protein rather than price per bag. If minimal processing is your real goal, remember that yogurt, eggs, milk and beans beat any powder; use powder for convenience, not as a substitute for food.
